  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Late arrivals join only new games; the host can track tables likely to finish and can keep a list for subsequent starts.\", \"decision\": \"How should late arrivals find a game that will start soon?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nTables post their likely finish times, and late arrivals choose a next-game waiting list beside a suitable table. Guests use visible timing information to decide which forthcoming opening best fits their interests and available time.\nA welcome volunteer introduces late arrivals to tables nearing completion and records any agreement to join the following game. A personal introduction establishes a likely next group while leaving the current game undisturbed.\nThe host adds late arrivals to a next-game list and approaches them when a suitable table becomes available. Guests can relax elsewhere without repeatedly checking whether current games have finished or seats have opened."
    }
  ],
